<% content_for :title, "Upload a console library" %>

<div class="admin-head">
  <div>
    <h1>Upload a console library</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Zip a console directory &mdash; the one holding <code>app/main.rb</code>
      and <code>app/console/</code> &mdash; and install it as a new version.
    </p>
  </div>
  <%= link_to "All versions", admin_console_versions_path, class: "secondary" %>
</div>

<%# Stated before the form, not in the help text under it, because it is the one
    rule that makes this safe and it is the one that will be the most annoying
    the first time somebody tries to fix a library in place. %>
<div class="admin-caution">
  <p>
    <strong>This installs a version that does not exist yet. It will not
    overwrite one that does.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Every cartridge is pinned to the library it was uploaded against, forever.
    Replacing an installed version would change the code those games run while
    leaving every pin looking intact &mdash; and a leaderboard whose runs stopped
    being comparable would not say so anywhere. To ship a change, bump the
    MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH constants in the library&rsquo;s own
    <code>app/console/version.rb</code> and upload it again.
  </p>
</div>

<%= form_with url: admin_console_versions_path, scope: :console_library_install,
      method: :post, class: "upload-form" do |f| %>
  <div class="field">
    <%= f.label :archive, "Console library (.zip)" %>
    <%= f.file_field :archive, accept: ".zip,application/zip", required: true %>
    <p class="muted">
      The archive may contain the library directory or be the library itself.
      Both are fine; two libraries in one archive is an error.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <%= f.label :title, "Title" %>
    <%= f.text_field :title, placeholder: "left blank, \"Console <version>\" is used" %>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <%= f.label :notes, "Notes" %>
    <%= f.text_field :notes, placeholder: "what changed in this version" %>
  </div>

  <%# Same reasoning as the cartridge upload form: a failed install re-renders
      with the problems, and a file input cannot be repopulated, so the error is
      shown as a pre-formatted block above instead. %>
  <%= f.submit "Install" %>
<% end %>

<div class="upload-help">
  <h2>What gets checked</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>app/main.rb</code> exists and requires at least one module under <code>app/console/</code>.</li>
    <li>Every module it requires is <strong>present in the archive</strong>. A missing one is a cartridge that boots and then fails.</li>
    <li>Every required path is a <code>.rb</code> module directly under <code>app/console/</code>. That require list is exactly what gets served to the browser for every cartridge on this version, so it cannot be used to add markup.</li>
    <li><code>app/console/version.rb</code> yields a MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH string, and that string names the version &mdash; an archive cannot be installed under a label it disagrees with.</li>
    <li>That version is not already installed, and no cartridge is pinned to it.</li>
    <li>No absolute paths, no <code>..</code> segments, no symlinks, and the archive cannot expand past 32MB or 512 files.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">
    The files are stored against the version row as Active Storage blobs, one per
    file, so <code>git status</code> stays clean and an upload is not a change to
    review. To change an installed version, bump MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH in
    <code>app/console/version.rb</code> and upload again.
  </p>
</div>